.TH WREX-ROUTING 7 "2026-10-18" "wrex 0.1.0" "wrex Manual"
.SH NAME
wrex-routing \- routing layer for \fBwrex\fR(1)

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwrex\fR \fIcraft\fR|\fIsend\fR [options] \fB--layer\fR \fIrouting\fR \fB--routing\-<field>\fR=\fIVALUE\fR ...
\fBwrex\fR \fIfields\fR \fIrouting\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
IPv6 routing header (RFC 8200 §4.4, next\-header 43): next_header + hdr_ext_len + routing type + segments left + the raw type\-specific region (zero\-padded to the 8\-octet grid on craft; the caller embeds the per\-type reserved prefix + 16\-byte addresses — e.g. RH0's 4 reserved bytes — verbatim on the wire). Dissection renders type/segs_left and the region raw; segs_left is NOT validated against the segment count (deliberate invalid packets are a feature). Typed per\-type decoding (type\-2 home address) is a deferral. len autofills (octets/8)\-1; explicit wins and is kept.
.

.SH ENCAPSULATION
Rank 25; stacks on ipv6, hopopts, routing, frag, dstopts, ah (parents).

.SH "FIELD FLAGS"
Dots in field paths become dashes in flags (ipv4.ttl -> --ipv4-ttl, --routing-next_header).
Explicit values always win over autofill and are kept
unvalidated; \fB\-\-strict\fR re-validates (violations exit 2).
.TP
\fB\-\-routing\-next_header=\fIINT\fR\fR
next header protocol (autofill: derived from the next layer; 59 = no next header) Type u8. Default: 59.
.TP
\fB\-\-routing\-len=\fIINT\fR\fR
hdr_ext_len: header length in 8\-octet units minus 1 (autofill: exact over the padded region) Type u8. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-routing\-type=\fIINT\fR\fR
routing type (0 = the deprecated RH0, 2 = home address) Type u8. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-routing\-segs_left=\fIINT\fR\fR
segments left (not validated against the segment count) Type u8. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-routing\-segments\fR
raw type\-specific region after the 4\-byte prefix (reserved bytes + 16\-byte addresses, hand\-built; hex on the CLI) Type bytes. Default: .

.SH EXAMPLES
wrex fields routing

